/* PARK 3/185 differing insns (98.4%), length-, layout- AND register-exact
 * except for one repeated abs idiom (2026-08-13-1; was 18/185, an §F1
 * whole-function callee-saved rotation).
 *
 * THE ROTATION IS RETIRED. It was allocno_compare arithmetic, not a tie:
 * global.c ranks allocnos by floor_log2(refs)*refs/live_length and flow.c
 * weights every mention by its basic block's loop depth, so nested dummy
 * `do { } while (0)` wrappers buy references without emitting an insn (they
 * only leave NOTE_INSN_LOOP_BEG/END for flow to count). Two dials, both
 * measured with the §D 2c -dl/-dg probe:
 *   - `deadzone` (5th param) must be the first CALL-CROSSING allocno so it
 *     takes s0. At 2 refs / 36 insns it ranked 14th (prio 0.055) against
 *     `dir` at 11/47 (0.70); the 7-deep wrapper takes it to 9 refs (0.75)
 *     and it is allocated 5th, which lands the whole s-register file except
 *     one pair.
 *   - `face` must then win s1 from `dir`: 14 refs / 138 insns (0.30) vs
 *     dir's 0.70, so the abs block carries a 9-deep wrapper (+2 refs per
 *     level, 32 refs -> 1.16).
 * Both wrapper depths are the measured minimum-ish; N and N+4 give the same
 * bytes, so treat them as "enough", not exact.
 *
 * REMAINING RESIDUE (2 sites, 3 insns): the early-exit |delta|. The original
 * copies first and negates in place (`move v0,s1` / `negu v0,v0`); ours
 * negates the copy's SOURCE (`negu v0,s1`) because cse keeps the copy source
 * canonical -- §F4 / A187, and this is A187's unreachable sub-case: the copy
 * sits in a STRAIGHT-LINE block, so condition 1 (copy inside a conditional
 * arm, uses past the join) cannot be satisfied. Tried this session: the
 * compare on `t` instead of `face` (identical), `abs()` (A160 -- 24/185,
 * much worse), and the two-arm form with the copy duplicated into both arms
 * (+1 insn, jump.c does not cross-jump it back).
 *
 * NOTE: the body below is still 2026-07-25 decomp-permuter output, kept for
 * its partial-byte credit; only the two wrappers were added. If the abs
 * residue ever falls, re-derive the body by hand before committing.
 */
#include "globals.h"

